1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:00,727
Hello!

2
00:00:00,727 --> 00:00:07,135
This week you will use your error log to find weak points, recognise four Listening traps,

3
00:00:07,135 --> 00:00:10,980
and learn three ways to recover when you are speaking.

4
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,251
Strategy one:

5
00:00:13,251 --> 00:00:16,237
read your error log before you practise.

6
00:00:16,237 --> 00:00:21,836
Give every wrong answer a label, such as spelling, plural, correction trap,

7
00:00:21,836 --> 00:00:23,553
or over the word limit.

8
00:00:23,553 --> 00:00:27,808
The label that appears most often is your first priority.

9
00:00:29,108 --> 00:00:30,079
Strategy two:

10
00:00:30,079 --> 00:00:31,647
four Listening traps.

11
00:00:31,647 --> 00:00:32,319
Trap one:

12
00:00:32,319 --> 00:00:37,919
when the speaker corrects the information, the answer is the final version.

13
00:00:37,919 --> 00:00:38,591
Trap two:

14
00:00:38,591 --> 00:00:44,564
when you hear used to or not any more, the thing that changed is often the trap.

15
00:00:45,864 --> 00:00:46,821
Twelve.

16
00:00:46,821 --> 00:00:50,784
Oh, sorry, actually fourteen.

17
00:00:54,084 --> 00:00:58,380
We used to lend aprons out, but we don't do that any more.

18
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:04,339
Trap three is spelling and plurals:

19
00:01:04,339 --> 00:01:06,847
missing an s can be marked wrong.

20
00:01:06,847 --> 00:01:08,974
Trap four is the word limit.

21
00:01:08,974 --> 00:01:12,165
If you lose an answer, don't keep waiting.

22
00:01:12,165 --> 00:01:16,344
Listen for the next signpost and find your place again.

23
00:01:17,644 --> 00:01:21,182
First of all, let's look at the background.

24
00:01:21,182 --> 00:01:23,404
Let's turn to the benefits.

25
00:01:26,704 --> 00:01:27,884
Strategy three:

26
00:01:27,884 --> 00:01:30,793
three ways to recover when you speak.

27
00:01:30,793 --> 00:01:31,108
One:

28
00:01:31,108 --> 00:01:34,882
use natural thinking phrases instead of silence.

29
00:01:34,882 --> 00:01:35,197
Two:

30
00:01:35,197 --> 00:01:39,365
if you forget a word, paraphrase it with other words.

31
00:01:39,365 --> 00:01:39,837
Three:

32
00:01:39,837 --> 00:01:45,184
if your answer is too short, extend it with a reason and an example.

33
00:01:46,484 --> 00:01:49,186
That's an interesting question.

34
00:01:49,186 --> 00:01:51,452
Let me think for a second.

35
00:01:54,752 --> 00:01:58,280
It's the thing you hold over your head when it rains.

36
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:02,588
Strategy four:

37
00:02:02,588 --> 00:02:08,060
record yourself with your phone or computer, because the app doesn't record.

38
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:13,316
Listen once to count the long pauses, and once to hear your word endings.

39
00:02:13,316 --> 00:02:16,196
Then re-record just your weakest answer.

40
00:02:17,496 --> 00:02:23,928
Yes, I listen to music almost every day, mainly because it makes my commute feel shorter.

41
00:02:27,228 --> 00:02:28,230
Common mistakes:

42
00:02:28,230 --> 00:02:33,239
writing the first number you hear without waiting for the speaker to correct it,

43
00:02:33,239 --> 00:02:38,436
dropping the plural s, and answering a Speaking question with one word such as Yes.

44
00:02:39,736 --> 00:02:42,195
Mini quiz, question one.

45
00:02:42,195 --> 00:02:43,117
You hear:

46
00:02:43,117 --> 00:02:46,191
Twenty, no, wait, twenty-five.

47
00:02:46,191 --> 00:02:49,264
Which number should you write?

48
00:02:52,564 --> 00:02:53,616
Question two.

49
00:02:53,616 --> 00:02:58,472
The instruction says ONE WORD ONLY, but you write two words,

50
00:02:58,472 --> 00:03:01,143
even though the meaning is right.

51
00:03:01,143 --> 00:03:03,004
Is that correct or not?

52
00:03:06,304 --> 00:03:07,650
Question three.

53
00:03:07,650 --> 00:03:10,609
You forget a word while speaking.

54
00:03:10,609 --> 00:03:14,018
Should you stay silent, or paraphrase?

55
00:03:14,018 --> 00:03:16,888
The answer is in the next scene.

56
00:03:20,188 --> 00:03:20,864
Answers.

57
00:03:20,864 --> 00:03:21,202
One:

58
00:03:21,202 --> 00:03:26,438
twenty-five, because the final information is the correct one.

59
00:03:26,438 --> 00:03:26,776
Two:

60
00:03:26,776 --> 00:03:31,000
not correct, because you went over the word limit.

61
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:31,506
Three:

62
00:03:31,506 --> 00:03:35,476
paraphrase, and don't stay silent for too long.

63
00:03:37,776 --> 00:03:38,311
Summary:

64
00:03:38,311 --> 00:03:43,059
practise the error label you make most, watch out for correction traps,

65
00:03:43,059 --> 00:03:46,002
and use the three speaking recovery methods.

66
00:03:46,002 --> 00:03:49,814
Remember that the mock test is our own shortened version,

67
00:03:49,814 --> 00:03:53,291
so the estimated band may be higher than in reality.

68
00:03:53,291 --> 00:03:56,568
The app does not guarantee your real exam result.
